    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d354">

                <pb facs="0432" n="320" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg320"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.51/295</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Assistant Secretary of the Treasury</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leffingwell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Counselor for the Department of State</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Polk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Polk</hi>: The Secretary of the Treasury is
                    intending to establish a credit of $15,000,000 in favor of the Republic of Cuba
                    and I will be obliged if you will advise this department whether the Republic of
                    Cuba has power to incur this indebtedness and whether the Cuban Minister has
                    authority to sign obligations for the amounts advanced. It is intended to take
                    Cuban demand obligations for the amounts advanced, secured by the pledge of
                    bonds of the Republic of Cuba authorized by the act of the Congress of Cuba of
                    July 31, 1917.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C. Leffingwell</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
